### Character Busy Check with Artisan
```lua
-- Check if character is busy (including Artisan)
function IsCharacterBusy()
    return Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.casting] or
           Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.betweenAreas] or
           Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.beingMoved] or
           Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.craftingMode] or
           Svc.Condition[CharacterCondition.executingCraftingSkill] or
           IsArtisanRunning() or
           Player.IsBusy
end
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Always Check Plugin Availability
```lua
-- Check if Artisan is available before use
if not HasPlugin("Artisan") then
    yield("/echo [Script] Artisan not available")
    return false
end
```

### 2. Use Timeouts for Crafting
```lua
-- Always use timeouts for crafting operations
if not WaitForArtisanComplete(300) then
    yield("/echo [Script] Crafting timeout")
    return false
end
```

### 3. Handle Crafting States
```lua
-- Check crafting state before starting new crafting
if IsArtisanRunning() then
    yield("/echo [Script] Artisan is already running")
    return true
end
```

### 4. Monitor Endurance Status
```lua
-- Monitor endurance status during crafting
if IPC.Artisan.GetEnduranceStatus() then
    yield("/echo [Script] Endurance is active")
end
```

### 5. Use Appropriate Wait Times
```lua
-- Use appropriate wait times for crafting monitoring
while IsArtisanRunning() do
    yield("/wait 1") -- Longer wait for crafting
end
```

